\[CapitalGamma],spectrum,h,G,\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[Phi]\\), \\(0\\)]\\),\
\[Epsilon]] computes the Casimir potential \\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(V\\), \
\\(Cas\\)]\\)(\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[Phi]\\), \\(0\\)]\\)) summing over \
all elements \[Gamma] \[Element] \[CapitalGamma], all lattice sums, including \
traces over all representations in the \
\\!\\(\\*StyleBox[\\\"spectrum\\\",\\nFontSlant->\\\"Italic\\\"]\\), and the \
appropriate numerical factors for each element, with default fermion boundary \
conditions given by the spin structure vector \\!\\(\\*OverscriptBox[\\(h\\), \
\\(\[Rule]\\)] = {\\*SubscriptBox[h, 1],...,\\*SubscriptBox[h, k]}\\) and \
evaluated at the point \\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[Phi]\\), \\(0\\)]\\) in \
moduli space given as the replacement rule \
{\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[Phi]\\), \\(i\\)]\\) \[Rule] \
